	<item>
		<title>By: Krista Cameron</title>
		<link>http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=390&#038;cpage=1#comment-13902</link>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Krista Cameron]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sat, 05 Jan 2013 10:06:57 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?page_id=390#comment-13902</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[This was my great uncle and I have so much admiration and respect and love for him. He was so strong in life, that he still shines through.

He was driving me to school one morning, fifth grade, in his vw rabbit with a dashboard of beautiful feathers and rocks....just enjoying the ride..to realize he was taking in the nature and beauty that we were going about 5 mph and had a traffic jam behind us buses, cars, you name it... He hardly sped up and led the parade to my school, where I got out and felt like the coolest kid ever...he really enriched my life and there will never be anyone like him.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>This was my great uncle and I have so much admiration and respect and love for him. He was so strong in life, that he still shines through.</p>
<p>He was driving me to school one morning, fifth grade, in his vw rabbit with a dashboard of beautiful feathers and rocks&#8230;.just enjoying the ride..to realize he was taking in the nature and beauty that we were going about 5 mph and had a traffic jam behind us buses, cars, you name it&#8230; He hardly sped up and led the parade to my school, where I got out and felt like the coolest kid ever&#8230;he really enriched my life and there will never be anyone like him.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
